mac os or a windows based laptop that is  the question that has always been on the  forefront of any media student video  editor photographer graphics designer  and practically almost anyone who has  been or still is in the creative  industry  most creatives have signed their souls  to the apple way of life and often have  decided swear off windows for good  like  creators like myself  but hey  having been raised on microsoft  operating systems i'm willing to give  this baby a chance  as a writer designer and video creative  myself  a laptop that maximizes productivity and  is easy to bring on the go at any given  time is a huge plus  and usually the decision lies between  choosing something that packs powerful  hardware versus something that is  extremely mobile and portable  that being said this takes the cake for  anyone looking for a windows based  macbook pro  hey guys it's abita here from geek  culture and this is the huawei mate book  x pro 2020 the huawei mate book x pro  first launched in 2018 and has won many  awards and accolades for its surprising  power precision and overall quality  suited for professionals and those in  creative lines of work  looking at the 2020 version nothing has  changed aesthetically the matebook x  it still looks like it's preceding  additions but it's more of a hardware  spec bump by no means is this  necessarily a bad thing as the saying  goes if it ain't broke don't fix it and  that is the ethos of what the matebook x  pro 2020 is trying to do  starting with the overall design and  build the macbook x pro is a good  looking and clean laptop it comes in a  gorgeous space gray aluminum chassis  along with sleek curved beveled edges on  the sides a well-positioned full-size  keyboard a large click pad and even a  fingerprint sensor that doubles as a  power on button  in terms of input and output a usba 3.0  we have the usual headphone jack and a  pair of usbcs that support all  thunderbolt 3 features  it also boasts a quad speaker system  firing through grilles on the side of  the keyboard and some cutouts in the  bottom panel these speakers are loud and  provide good sound all these come  packaged in a very compact 14.6  millimeters or just short of 5 8 of an  inch thick  and weighing approximately 1.33  kilograms or under three pounds making  this ultrabook one that is portable and  comfortable to take anywhere  in fact those in particular believe how  this passed the one-handed opening test  what brings the whole thing together is  its stunning 13.9 inch nearly bezel-less  display a whopping 91 screen to body  ratio  this 3000 by 2000 resolution  260 pixel per inch display offers a  different aspect ratio of 3x2 than a  conventional 16x9 widescreen aspect  ratio we see in conventional laptops  this gives much better productivity due  to more real estate whether it's typing  out a document or working on a design  the hundred percent srgb white color  gamut also makes images and videos more  vibrant and the details more vivid  which is perfect for creatives in terms  of color accuracy  better yet the display itself is touch  screen with gesture control that allows  you to scroll  zoom select and even swipe down with  three fingers to capture the screen  effortlessly if you're not the type to  smudge your screen the large click pad  provides excellent precision and click  feel the white backlit keyboard also  gives satisfaction with a combination of  1.2 millimeters travel and a subtle soft  click once fully depressed another thing  to note is that the keyboard is splash  proof which is a very good plus  one feature that took us by surprise is  the webcam on the laptop hidden  underneath a key in the function button  row  it is a nifty and smart design to avoid  adding more space on the screen it's a  clever way of hiding the camera and you  can simply store it away when you don't  want to be seen guess that means no one  sticking tape over the camera and  further ruining the quality of your  webcam big plus there  [Music]  however the camera's position makes it  an unflattering angle for some and when  it comes to zoom calls  you can forget typing while on call as  your knuckles will get in the way  it's also not the best front camera you  would have  sporting only one megapixel  don't expect crisp images or videos  unless you're creative who depends on  good webcam like a vlogger or a cam girl  for example  the webcam gets the job done  the microphone sensitivity is  decent in fact  relying up fall microphones to  accurately pick up sound and small feet  away  with all these features and the hardware  this baby packs some pretty awesome  performance specs for an ultrabook  the latest 10th gen intel i7 processor  nvidia geforce mx250  16 gigabytes  lpddr3 ram  one terabyte ssd  all these specs make this the everyday  machine powerful enough to bear the  grunt work like photoshop 1080p video  editing on premiere pro and even casual  gaming  which few ultrabooks can do with ease  all other productivity tasks will run  here with no hiccups  running on windows 10 home edition the  matebook x pro does not come with  bloatware with only proprietary huawei  ads like huawei share and huawei pc  manager  just like apple has its eyedrop huawei  hasn't emerged with its own  the huawei share app allows huawei phone  users to utilize high speed direct file  and data transfer with a simple tab with  its dedicated nfc zone and simply drag  and drop with a touchscreen has made the  task a lot more convenient  not only that the huawei share app can  also be used as a multi-screen  collaboration conveniently popping up a  mirrored cast of your phone onto your  laptop allowing you to put your phone  down and multitask all within the laptop  itself  next comes the huge 56 watt hour battery  boasting up to 13 hours of video  playback 11 hours of web browsing and 15  hours of light to moderate work  all in a single charge  plenty of battery for a busy work day or  even a long flight and if 13 hours is  not good enough  the 65 watt usb c charging provides  blazing fast charging at a full hundred  percent for an average of 90 minutes  while inactive  the key takeaway is the lack of a power  brick like many conventional laptops  have  another great convenience in terms of  portability and space  if you're looking for further expansion  say  hooking it up to an external monitor the  matebook x pro comes bundled with a  matebook dock 2.0 right of the box  on top of that you can also buy some  accompanying accessories like the huawei  bluetooth mouse swift and the huawei  backpack swift  isn't really that great some of you  might be thinking to yourselves well  yeah there are a few downsides if you  want me to be nitpicky about it for a  laptop that's targeted for creatives  there's no sd card slot which is just a  bummer to say the least  the lack of hardware customization  options is also a factor that might  potentially put off those interested in  the matebook x pro  especially with only one terabyte of  storage space it might not last very  long if you want a laptop that has  macbook performance a laptop running a  windows 10 with support portability  this  is definitely a heavy hitter the huawei  mate book x pro is out in singapore and  it's priced at two thousand six hundred  and ninety eight dollars  [Music]
 

